releases.body:
### What this release delivers

The SPL Associated Token Account program (`ATokenGPvbdGVxr1b2hvZbsiqW5xWH25efTNsLJA8knL`) was the **#1 acquisition gap** in the ecosystem measurement (`research/ecosystem-coverage-2026-11-11.json`): **1,410 payloads across 6 finalized mainnet blocks, with no IDL account published at either pullable address**.

This release ships a derived wire table for the ATA program, derived directly from the vendored upstream Rust sources (`solana-program/associated-token-account@fbf5379`, Apache-2.0, LICENSE + sha256 pin on all three files).

### Install

```bash
npm install github:auroraxo/sememe#v0.4.18   # tagged release; no npm account needed
```

### What changed

- `src/ata-interface.mjs`: derives the wire table from upstream TEXT (instruction builder literals cross-checked against the declaration index the borsh derive uses; processor empty-input Create fallback and InvalidInstructionData refusal);
- `src/ata.mjs`: two-check load (fresh derivation + artifact equality), exported as `sememe/ata`;
- CLI: `sememe decode-ata <program> [<payload>] [--empty]` and `sememe ata-provenance`;
- `sememe decode` now points at `decode-ata` instead of telling the user to pull a receipt that cannot exist;
- Package exports `./ata`, description updated.

### Evidence

- **1,410/1,410 ATA payloads decode** from the committed 6-block sample (`research/ecosystem-coverage-2026-11-11.json`), 1,406 byte-exact; 4 empty payloads are named Create via the processor's own fallback and honestly carry `roundTripByteExact: false`;
- Ecosystem coverage moves from **75.6% -> 82.2%** (watchlist 96.4% unchanged, outside-watchlist **7.1% -> 35.4%**); `no-interface` **3,944 -> 2,534**;
- The 1,000-transaction foreign-archive wire sweep decodes **5,032** payloads (was 4,646) with zero disagreements;
- `test/ata-interface.test.mjs` (8 tests): tampered artifact, tampered vendored source, missing vendor all refuse the load; guards prove ATA stays out of the token table and SPL Token is undisturbed;
- Suite 825 -> 833 (829 pass / 4 named network skips / 0 fail).

### Limits

No external users yet (0 non-owner stars/forks/issues/PRs); not an audit; own-host measurement on committed finalized blocks. No account list or PDA derivation is claimed — only instruction data. Tags are immutable; older tags retain the acquisition gap.
